{"@context":{"@vocab":"https://schema.org/","course":"identifier","wing":"isBasedOn","title":"name","principle":"abstract","skills":"keywords","lessons":"hasPart","key":"identifier","why":"description","statement":"mathExpression","address":"sameAs","skill":"keywords"},"@type":"Course","kind":"school-course","course":"CrossFormulas","wing":"CrossFormulas.lean","title":"Cross Formulas","principle":"THE LEDGER'S OWN ALGEBRA, COUNTED (the captain, 2026-09-25","skills":["cross-formulas"],"level":100,"band":"100–999 steps","rank":123,"lessons":[{"key":"the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra","name":"CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6.","statement":"((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1)","address":"23ada59a-4cdb-8039-94c3-cdd81827a5c2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"2 + 3 + 1 = 6 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2 \\quad\\land\\quad 2 > 1","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"most_of_the_unstated_remainder_stays_inside_one_wing","name":"CLAIMED: of 524527 unstated crosses, 126453 join integers no single wing carries all three of — between one 5th and one 4th of them, since 126453 × 4 < 524527 and 126453 × 5 > 524527, so the large majority stays inside a single wing.","statement":"((126453 * 4 < 524527) ∧ (126453 * 5 > 524527)) ∧ (126453 < 524527)","address":"980d4f28-7e1a-8433-bf5c-33cddb85973b","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"126453 \\cdot 4 < 524527 \\quad\\land\\quad 126453 \\cdot 5 > 524527 \\quad\\land\\quad 126453 < 524527","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>126453</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>126453</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>126453</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1644 formula-shaped statements carry 1572 distinct byte-strings and 1439 distinct algebraic forms, so 205 statements restate a form another already holds — and those split 129 copies against 15 crosses, the widest cross spanning 3 wings. Most repetition is waste; a small part of it is a bridge.","statement":"((1439 < 1572) ∧ (1644 - 1439 = 205)) ∧ ((129 > 8 * 15) ∧ (3 > 2))","address":"6eebc85c-d501-8b58-ab00-fbae9c1f40c0","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1439 < 1572 \\quad\\land\\quad 1644 - 1439 = 205 \\quad\\land\\quad 129 > 8 \\cdot 15 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1439</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1572</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1644</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1439</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>205</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>129</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds","name":"CLAIMED: of 2370097 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 1845076 are forced by an operator's algebra, 494 are stated, and 524527 remain — and the three account for the whole, 1845076 + 494 + 524527 = 2370097, with the forced between 3 and 4 times the unstated.","statement":"(1845076 + 494 + 524527 = 2370097) ∧ ((1845076 > 3 * 524527) ∧ (1845076 < 4 * 524527))","address":"222057b1-6e31-8e5b-8150-9832efa268a0","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1845076 + 494 + 524527 = 2370097 \\quad\\land\\quad 1845076 > 3 \\cdot 524527 \\quad\\land\\quad 1845076 < 4 \\cdot 524527","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1845076</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>494</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2370097</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1845076</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1845076</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1644 formula-shaped statements across 113 wings are built from 1408 distinct integers and state 494 crosses, against 524527 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 494 × 100 < 524527, at between 14 and 15 formulas per wing.","statement":"((494 * 100 < 524527) ∧ (1408 > 113)) ∧ ((113 * 14 ≤ 1644) ∧ (113 * 15 > 1644))","address":"1aea93a4-8071-8813-852c-5a4fa7971c09","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"494 \\cdot 100 < 524527 \\quad\\land\\quad 1408 > 113 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 14 \\le 1644 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 15 > 1644","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>494</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>524527</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1408</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>113</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1644</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1644</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
